# Paths clang-format must never touch. Honored by the editor (format-on-save),
# the clang-format CLI, and any CI format gate — a single, reproducible exception list.
#
# GROUND RULE: never reformat external or vendored code. Keeping these byte-for-byte
# as upstream is what lets us diff our ports against the originals.
#
# Patterns are globs; `*` stops at a path separator, so `**` is required to match a
# whole subtree (clang-format 18+ semantics).


# NOTHING first-party is excluded any more. The engine was listed here because it
# was imported verbatim and the diff against upstream was the only way to review
# it. That diff has since been spent deliberately -- the engine is renamed,
# namespaced and restructured -- so there is nothing left to protect. Leaving it
# listed only hid the engine from clang-format while the format gate reported
# success on files it never opened.
